      gotchas: [
        "RPO and RTO are REQUIREMENTS (the SLO), not features. Service capabilities must MEET the RPO/RTO target.",
        "Cross-region replication in Azure is mostly ASYNC (SQL geo-replication, GRS, ASR). RPO 0 across regions needs synchronous/strong designs; RPO 0 for zone failure = zone redundancy.",
        "Availability Zones and Availability Sets are mutually exclusive on a single VM. Pick one. AZs preferred for new builds.",
        "ZRS protects against zone failure, NOT regional failure. Don't confuse with GRS.",
        "GRS to ZRS is a TWO-STEP change (GRS → LRS, then LRS → ZRS conversion). It can take a long time.",
        "RA-GRS/RA-GZRS let you read the secondary endpoint any time without failing over.",
        "ASR (Azure-to-Azure): crash-consistent recovery points every 5 minutes (fixed); app-consistent snapshots are optional with configurable frequency.",
        "ASR test failover into an isolated VNet = zero production impact. Always test before real failover.",
        "Multi-tier app failover in the right order with scripts = ASR recovery plan (boot groups + runbooks).",
        "Backup soft delete: 14-180 days (first 14 free), enforced on Recovery Services vaults. MUA adds Resource Guard approval.",
        "'Backups must not be deletable by anyone, even admins, for X years' = immutable vault (locked) + retention policy + soft delete + MUA.",
        "Up to 500 vaults (Recovery Services + Backup) per subscription.",
        "Recovery point retention: up to 9999 points per protected instance.",
        "MARS agent: file/folder/system state backup from on-prem Windows. No bare-metal restore. MARS doesn't replace ASR — backup vs replication are different.",
        "Azure Files backups (snapshot or vaulted) live in a Recovery Services vault. Disks/blobs/PostgreSQL/AKS use a Backup vault.",
        "Azure SQL DB/MI and Cosmos DB backups are built into the service — no vault to deploy.",
        "Failover Group provides read-write + read-only listener endpoints. Apps don't change connection strings after failover.",
        "Failover Group != Active Geo-Replication. Geo-replication is per-DB, manual failover, no listener (up to 4 secondaries).",
        "Cheapest SQL DR with relaxed RPO/RTO = geo-restore from geo-redundant backups. Tight RPO/RTO = failover group.",
        "SQL Server on-prem needing a cloud DR replica without building VMs = Managed Instance link to SQL MI.",
        "Cosmos DB multi-region writes: any region accepts writes. Conflict resolution: last-writer-wins by default, custom via stored procedure.",
        "Cosmos accidental delete recovery to any second in the last 7 days at no backup storage cost = continuous backup 7-day tier.",
        "Blob point-in-time restore needs soft delete + versioning + change feed; works on block blobs in GPv2 standard accounts, not HNS/ADLS Gen2.",
        "Object replication and GRS replicate deletes/corruption too. They are durability, not backup — pair with soft delete/versioning/immutability.",
        "Cross-tenant Azure Backup: not supported. Same Entra tenant required for backup operations (Resource Guard for MUA can be in another tenant).",
        "Site Recovery for Azure VMs normally targets another region; zone-to-zone DR (same region) is also supported in select regions.",
        "Always On availability groups on SQL VMs: listener via Standard internal load balancer, or deploy replicas in multiple subnets to avoid the LB.",
        "Service Bus Geo-DR copies only metadata (entities), not messages. Need messages replicated = Service Bus Geo-Replication (Premium).",
        "AKS backup = Azure Backup for AKS (Backup vault + extension). Images in DR region = ACR geo-replication (Premium).",
        "Don't rely on paired regions blindly: newer regions may have no pair, and Microsoft-managed geo-failover is a last resort — plan customer-managed failover.",
      ],
